{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Can someone finally tell me how to forward specific lab baskets to a covering physician when doctors are out of office? The documentation is useless and this is slowing us down tremendously.",
   "id": "gen-031",
   "subject": "Routing lab results to covering physicians"
  },
  {
   "body": "I cannot find any way to add a custom pharmacy entry when the directory doesn't list a local compounder our patients use. Why is this basic feature so hard to locate?",
   "id": "gen-032",
   "subject": "Missing pharmacy in directory / custom entries"
  },
  {
   "body": "Every time I try to run the batch for clearinghouse submission, it rejects half our claims with vague error codes. How are we supposed to fix these validation issues quickly?",
   "id": "gen-033",
   "subject": "Clearinghouse validation errors on claim batch"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am so sorry to bother you with this, but I made a terrible mess of posting our latest remittance advice. When a check covers multiple patients and invoice lines, I keep misapplying the payments and my ledger is completely out of balance. I tried reversing the deposit batch to start over, but it locked the entries. Could someone please help me figure out how to safely clear out these incorrect lines and reapply them properly?",
   "id": "gen-034",
   "subject": "Apologies - need help correcting misapplied payments across multiple invoice lines"
  },
  {
   "body": "We need to limit online scheduling so patients can only book certain visit types with specific doctors. Right now everything is wide open and it's causing chaos at the front desk. Please advise how to restrict this.",
   "id": "gen-035",
   "subject": "Restricting online booking options"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am writing because we had a serious incident involving medication substitution alerts. Earlier today, while trying to handle an out-of-stock pharmacy notification, a screen popped up that appeared to display another patient's active medication history and pharmacy profile instead of the chart I was working in. Our staff caught it quickly, but we are extremely concerned about a potential data privacy leak between records. I have locked the terminal and noted the exact time this occurred. We need an urgent review of how these substitution workflows pull up patient context to ensure this does not happen again.",
   "id": "gen-036",
   "subject": "URGENT: Cross-patient data visibility during medication substitution alert"
  },
  {
   "body": "Patients are sitting in the exam rooms waiting and I am completely blocked. Every time I try to switch a prescription due to a pharmacy out-of-stock alert, the system errors out or loops me back to the main chart. I need this fixed immediately so I can send these out.",
   "id": "gen-037",
   "subject": "CRITICAL: Cannot process medication substitution, patients waiting"
  },
  {
   "body": "I'm so sorry to submit another ticket, but I am struggling with the validation errors on our latest insurance batch. Could someone take a quick look when you have a moment and guide me on how to clear them out before submission?",
   "id": "gen-038",
   "subject": "Sorry for reaching out - claim batch validation questions"
  },
  {
   "body": "We need to update the text template used for monthly patient statements. Can you point me to where we edit the reminder language before the next batch goes out?",
   "id": "gen-039",
   "subject": "Editing monthly billing statement templates"
  },
  {
   "body": "I'm so sorry to bother support with this, but we are trying to set up our online booking portal and want to restrict certain visit types. Could you please send over a quick walkthrough on how to limit bookings to specific providers?",
   "id": "gen-040",
   "subject": "Sorry to ask - online booking provider restrictions"
  }
 ]
}
